# github-mcp - environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the same directory. `.env` is gitignored.
# Values here are examples; replace with real credentials locally and
# never commit them.

# Personal Access Token used for authenticated GitHub API calls. Fine-
# grained tokens are recommended; the minimum required scopes are:
#   - Contents:  Read and write
#   - Metadata:  Read-only (auto-selected)
# For classic tokens: the "repo" scope covers the same surface.
#
# This is the same env var Cursor's official github-mcp-server reads,
# so a machine-scoped user env var works for both. The github-mcp
# server also accepts a per-request `token` argument on each tool call;
# when supplied, the argument wins over this env var.
GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Optional fallback env var. When GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN is unset,
# the server checks GITHUB_TOKEN next.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
